Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:17:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 089/154] feat(window): Cmd+Shift+W closes the window the user
 selected
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cmd+Shift+W is matched on the raw NSEvent, because the File menu item behind
it is an AppKit performClose: item that AppKit alone validates. It resolves
the window off the event rather than off the visible tab's Browser, which
under a presenter swap belongs to a different, off-screen window.

The red traffic light and File > Close Window arrive at windowShouldClose:
rather than through Widget::CloseWithReason, so the client view now routes
them back to the window and they count as user-initiated too. That override
beats the last-tab-out keep-open, survives a beforeunload prompt the user
cancels, and is re-armed per close since CloseWithReason spends it.

The keep-open gate and the AppKit close choice move to
atrium_window_close_decision, so both can be asserted without a Browser, a
widget or an NSWindow. ParseCombo now refuses the chords the dispatcher
claims, so no action can be bound to one and silently shadowed.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
